title: theil_decomposition
---



```python
theil_decomposition(
    data,
    variable,
    by=None,
    *,
    permutations=0,
    seed=12345,
    title=None,
    ref=None,
)
```

Theil's index split in two: inequality between groups of units and inequality within them.

## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}

| Name         | Type        | Description                                                                                                                                                                                            | Default    |
|--------------|-------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|
| data         |             | A dataset id, or a panel with ``geo_id`` and ``year``, e.g. from ``load``                                                                                                                              | _required_ |
| variable     | str         | The numeric column to measure, in levels and strictly positive                                                                                                                                         | _required_ |
| by           | str \| None | The groups: a column of the table, or a coarser scale the units nest in (see ``ancestors``). Default: the coarsest such scale with two or more units. A unit must stay in the same group in every year | `None`     |
| permutations | int         | Random reassignments of units to groups behind the pseudo p-value of the between component (0: no test)                                                                                                | `0`        |
| seed         | int         | Makes the permutations reproducible                                                                                                                                                                    | `12345`    |
| title        | str \| None | The figure title                                                                                                                                                                                       | `None`     |

## Returns {.doc-section .doc-section-returns}

| Name   | Type        | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
|--------|-------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        | TheilResult | A result with ``.df`` (one row per year: ``theil``, ``between``, ``within``, which add up to it, ``between_share``, and ``p_between`` with permutations), ``.fig`` (the two components stacked, with the between share), ``.gt``, ``.by``, ``.n_groups``, ``.notes`` and ``.interpret()``. |

## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}

```python
!pip install -q geo4bolivia
import geo4bolivia as geo

res = geo.theil_decomposition("sdg", "index_sdg", by="department")
print(res.interpret())
res.fig
```

