The Theil index of **Sustainable Development Index, IDS (0-100)** splits additively into inequality **between** the 9 department groups and inequality **within** them (between + within = total, exactly).

In the latest year (2024), the total Theil index is 0.00381: about 15% of it lies between department groups and 85% within them — most inequality plays out among units inside the same department.

Over the window, the between-group share fell from 20% to 15% — group means are pulling closer together relative to the differences inside groups.

_These are associations, not causal effects. A causal reading needs a research design._
